sibility, attention, but hot temper and know-it-all attitude affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some issues. Which candidate has the best balance? B has strong reliability and stress, but communication issues. C has strong decision, stress, crew concern, but communication and egocentric. D has strong problem solving, responsibility, but hot temper. A has technical and leadership but not open to new ideas and show-off.\n\nWhich is most critical? For long-distance pilot, crew cooperation and communication are vital. B's nasty remarks may be severe. C's egocentric and communication difficulty also problematic, but his concern for others may mitigate. D's hot temper also severe. A's show-off may be less severe than others? But lack of openness to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nThus candidate C might be best overall: decision quality, calmness, technical, crew concern, despite communication difficulty. B's reliability is high but his nasty remarks could be dangerous. I'd lean to C.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate C, referencing prior discussion (maybe referencing Agent 1's recommendation of B). I will argue that while B is reliable, his communication issues outweigh his strengths, and C's decision quality and crew concern make him better.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
